> From September 27 to October 5, 2026, the 14.2 refinement work ran the preregistered studies PREREG16 to PREREG45 (with PREREG28b) against the 14.1 benchmark record. **No engine file, coefficient or default of the shipped 14.1 was changed by any of them, and 14.1 remains the release.** The work produced an adopted scoring convention (volume under C1, or C2 where tags allow), an adopted scorer revision (r2, from PREREG37 on), one regional NS candidate that passes its benchmark gates but has not cleared a Bakuzis grid (v141LTfi), and named failures that locate the remaining NS and QC errors. The QC height anchor track is closed with the shipped 0.111 kept for 14.2: a field tag anchor (1.242) corrects QC height increment on the benchmark and passes a top height gate on measured heights against the 10% FIA measurement quality objective for tree length, but it fails the published TOPHT gate and does not clear the Bakuzis QC grid (PREREG38 to PREREG41), and the earlier QC height gates built on row index pairs are corrected by an erratum (PREREG42). The origin of 0.111 is now traced: no record fits it, and it was set by hand from the rounded console output of a July 2026 stand level top height diagnostic (PREREG43). A Bakuzis QC grid started from measured stand lists (PREREG44) does not clear 1.242 either, and its reported trajectories show that neither scalar gives a credible long run height path, which points 14.3 at the QC height increment form. PREREG45 tested that form for 14.3: a per year relative height multiplier, exp(a + b HT/ESI) fitted on fold A field tags, is the first QC arm to pass every benchmark gate on held out field tags, the published TOPHT gate included, but over 100 years its top height still rises past the measured stand frontier and it adds two Reineke flags, so it is not a 14.3 candidate as specified. Each gated verdict follows a decision rule fixed before any held out value was read, and the one post hoc step, the PREREG21 split of its survivor term, is declared as such in that RESULT.
54a55,56
> PREREG45, for 14.3 only, replaced the QC scalar with m(r) = exp(a + b r), r = HT/ESI, reassigned to every tree each year. Fitted on the 698 fold A field tag survivors, a = 0.9595 and b = -1.1239, so m falls from 1.97 at r 0.25 to 0.74 at r 1.125. On screened qc_c fold B (737 field tags) the pooled predicted over observed increment ratio is 1.003 (0.897 to 1.143), the three diameter class biases are +0.002, +0.002 and -0.014 m yr⁻¹, every relative height bin is within 0.04 m yr⁻¹ (worst +0.030), the published TOPHT bias is +14.14% against the +14.63% limit and the dominant cohort reaches 0.980 of measured t2 height, so every benchmark gate passes, the first QC arm to do so. From the 36 measured PREREG44 stand lists, median top height over ESI goes from 0.784 to 1.163 at 50 years and 1.309 at 100, above the 99th percentile of measured QC stands (1.175) in 32 of 36 stands and still gaining about 1 m per 20 years, and Reineke flags two stands that 0.111 does not. The verdict is Rule 4, not cleared on long run grounds. The multiplier is positive at every relative height, so it slows height growth without stopping it; a form with a zero or an asymptote is the evident next arm. qc_rh also removes most of the top height falls that flag 0.111 (9 stands against 36). An NB arm was chosen but not run, since NB tree numbers are not stable tags and the field tag fit cannot be applied (PREREG32).
