> - The QC height increment form for 14.3, since from measured stand lists 0.111 stalls top height and 1.242 lets it rise to 1.5 times ESI and still climbing at 100 years (PREREG44). PREREG37 already shows why: on field tags observed over predicted increment falls from 1.655 below HT/ESI 0.5 to 0.523 at 1 to 1.25, while the coded `dht` has no relative height term. PREREG45 fitted a relative height multiplier that corrects the increment on held out tags but, being positive at every relative height, does not bound top height; the next arm is a form with a zero or an asymptote. The NB arm needs a stand level fit (PREREG45b, pending Aaron's choice).
